<title>GERMANY: Germans seek to export 25,000 T intervention rye.</title>
<headline>Germans seek to export 25,000 T intervention rye.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>German grain traders placed bids to export 25,000 tonnes of rye from intervention stores to third countries, state grain intervention board BLE said on Thursday.</p>
<p>BLE received no bids for the export of intervention wheat or barley.</p>
<p>--Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
